# Battery Limit Toggler

A simple GUI to toggle the battery charging limit (conservation mode) on Lenovo IdeaPad laptops running on Linux Mint.

Build:  ./build.sh   	  - needs gcc (or clang, but I havent tried it) and libx11-dev
Run:    ./dist/main       - may ask for your password when toggling

The conservation mode path is _hardcoded_ in main.c and may be different on other laptops.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Manual commands:

# Find battery charging limit info
# 1 - On
# 0 - Off
cat /sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:1f.0/PNP0C09:00/VPC2004:00/conservation_mode

# Disable battery charging limit
echo 0 | sudo tee /sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:1f.0/PNP0C09:00/VPC2004:00/conservation_mode

# Enable battery charging limit
echo 1 | sudo tee /sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:1f.0/PNP0C09:00/VPC2004:00/conservation_mode